/**
 * Which value ids of a byte-exact value store denote the same RDF term and must be merged (see
 * {@link LmdbLanguageTagVariantMerge}). Computed from the value store alone by
 * {@link ValueStore#planLanguageTagVariantMerge()}, so an interrupted merge re-plans the same merge on the next open.
 * <p>
 * A <em>losing</em> id is replaced by its <em>surviving</em> id everywhere and then deleted: every language literal of
 * a group of case variants of one term except the smallest id, and every triple term that becomes equal to another one
 * once its components are replaced by their survivors (again except the smallest id). A surviving triple term whose
 * stored components still mention a losing id keeps its id and has its components rewritten.
 */
